+# Launcher logbook
+
+## 2026-10-01 — Muse v3 transport and upstream launch bounds (TASK-261001-3fgu9f)
+
+- Muse maps to system `muse` and ax provider `muse` under the binding task decision. The v3 fragment carries four XDG parents under one managed home; `HOME` remains inherited. No prompt or MCP channel is admitted.
+- agents-management v0.5.33 supplies declaration-owned Muse model rows and explicitly permits their use by its system-only BuildLaunch path. Defaults now uses those rows without asserting a vendor binding; missing system/model authority still refuses.
+- The pinned module has no release-pinned Muse permission mapping, including native mode. The real launcher therefore currently refuses with `permission_mode_unsupported` before plan admission.
+- Separately, real `plan.Build` refuses with `plan_refused: spawn plane refused the launch: agentic: system does not support launch mode: muse does not declare interactive`. The test switches to admission when a pinned plugin declares interactive support. The launcher does not substitute exec/serve mode or rebuild provider argv.
+- Pin upgrade effect: the Claude plugin adds the owned literal `CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_PROMPT_SUGGESTION=false`; two launcher goldens now record it. The v1/v2 fragment schemas and reader contracts remain unchanged.
+- Windows vet fails on both the checkout baseline and this candidate: existing POSIX process-control and Mkfifo test code is not Windows-compilable. This gate is reported red, not waived as green.
